# Second DCM Identity by Direct Matrix Multiplication (Planar \(z\)-axis rotation)

Goal: explicitly compute \(C_i^{\,B}\ddot C_B^{\,i}\) and show

\[
C_i^{\,B}\ddot C_B^{\,i} = [\dot\omega]^\times + \big([\omega]^\times\big)^2
\]

for a rotation about the \(z\)-axis by \(\theta(t)\).

---

## 1) Write down \(C_i^{\,B}\) and \(C_B^{\,i}\)

Let \(c=\cos\theta(t)\), \(s=\sin\theta(t)\).

Given:

\[
C_i^{\,B}=
\begin{bmatrix}
c & s & 0\\
-s & c & 0\\
0&0&1
\end{bmatrix}
\]

Transpose to get:

\[
C_B^{\,i}=(C_i^{\,B})^T=
\begin{bmatrix}
c & -s & 0\\
s & c & 0\\
0&0&1
\end{bmatrix}
\]

---

## 2) Differentiate twice to get \(\ddot C_B^{\,i}\)

First derivatives (chain rule):

\[
\dot c = -\dot\theta\, s,
\qquad
\dot s = \dot\theta\, c
\]

So

\[
\dot C_B^{\,i}=
\begin{bmatrix}
-\dot\theta\, s & -\dot\theta\, c & 0\\
\dot\theta\, c & -\dot\theta\, s & 0\\
0&0&0
\end{bmatrix}
\]

Now differentiate entry-by-entry again. Useful second derivatives:

\[
\ddot c = -\ddot\theta\, s - \dot\theta^2\, c,
\qquad
\ddot s = \ddot\theta\, c - \dot\theta^2\, s
\]

But it’s easiest to directly differentiate each entry of \(\dot C_B^{\,i}\):

- \(\frac{d}{dt}(-\dot\theta s)= -\ddot\theta s - \dot\theta(\dot s)= -\ddot\theta s - \dot\theta(\dot\theta c)= -\ddot\theta s - \dot\theta^2 c\)
- \(\frac{d}{dt}(-\dot\theta c)= -\ddot\theta c - \dot\theta(\dot c)= -\ddot\theta c - \dot\theta(-\dot\theta s)= -\ddot\theta c + \dot\theta^2 s\)
- \(\frac{d}{dt}(\dot\theta c)= \ddot\theta c + \dot\theta(\dot c)= \ddot\theta c + \dot\theta(-\dot\theta s)= \ddot\theta c - \dot\theta^2 s\)
- \(\frac{d}{dt}(-\dot\theta s)= -\ddot\theta s - \dot\theta^2 c\)

Thus

\[
\ddot C_B^{\,i}=
\begin{bmatrix}
-\ddot\theta\, s - \dot\theta^2\, c
&
-\ddot\theta\, c + \dot\theta^2\, s
& 0\\
\ddot\theta\, c - \dot\theta^2\, s
&
-\ddot\theta\, s - \dot\theta^2\, c
& 0\\
0&0&0
\end{bmatrix}
\]

---

## 3) Multiply \(C_i^{\,B}\ddot C_B^{\,i}\) explicitly

Compute

\[
C_i^{\,B}\ddot C_B^{\,i}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
c & s & 0\\
-s & c & 0\\
0&0&1
\end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix}
-\ddot\theta\, s - \dot\theta^2\, c
&
-\ddot\theta\, c + \dot\theta^2\, s
& 0\\
\ddot\theta\, c - \dot\theta^2\, s
&
-\ddot\theta\, s - \dot\theta^2\, c
& 0\\
0&0&0
\end{bmatrix}
\]

### Entry (1,1)

\[
c(-\ddot\theta s-\dot\theta^2 c)+s(\ddot\theta c-\dot\theta^2 s)
=
-\ddot\theta cs-\dot\theta^2 c^2+\ddot\theta sc-\dot\theta^2 s^2
=
-\dot\theta^2(c^2+s^2)
=
-\dot\theta^2
\]

### Entry (1,2)

\[
c(-\ddot\theta c+\dot\theta^2 s)+s(-\ddot\theta s-\dot\theta^2 c)
=
-\ddot\theta(c^2+s^2)+\dot\theta^2(cs-sc)
=
-\ddot\theta
\]

### Entry (2,1)

\[
(-s)(-\ddot\theta s-\dot\theta^2 c)+c(\ddot\theta c-\dot\theta^2 s)
=
\ddot\theta(s^2+c^2)+\dot\theta^2(sc-cs)
=
\ddot\theta
\]

### Entry (2,2)

\[
(-s)(-\ddot\theta c+\dot\theta^2 s)+c(-\ddot\theta s-\dot\theta^2 c)
=
\ddot\theta(sc-cs)-\dot\theta^2(s^2+c^2)
=
-\dot\theta^2
\]

All third-row/third-column entries are zero.

Therefore

\[
C_i^{\,B}\ddot C_B^{\,i}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
-\dot\theta^2 & -\ddot\theta & 0\\
\ddot\theta & -\dot\theta^2 & 0\\
0&0&0
\end{bmatrix}
\]

---

## 4) Compute the RHS: \([\dot\omega]^\times + ([\omega]^\times)^2\)

For a \(z\)-axis rotation:

\[
\boldsymbol\omega=
\begin{bmatrix}
0\\0\\\dot\theta
\end{bmatrix},
\qquad
\dot{\boldsymbol\omega}=
\begin{bmatrix}
0\\0\\\ddot\theta
\end{bmatrix}
\]

Cross-product matrices:

\[
[\omega]^\times=
\begin{bmatrix}
0 & -\dot\theta & 0\\
\dot\theta & 0 & 0\\
0&0&0
\end{bmatrix},
\qquad
[\dot\omega]^\times=
\begin{bmatrix}
0 & -\ddot\theta & 0\\
\ddot\theta & 0 & 0\\
0&0&0
\end{bmatrix}
\]

Square \( [\omega]^\times \):

\[
([\omega]^\times)^2
=
\begin{bmatrix}
0 & -\dot\theta & 0\\
\dot\theta & 0 & 0\\
0&0&0
\end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix}
0 & -\dot\theta & 0\\
\dot\theta & 0 & 0\\
0&0&0
\end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
-\dot\theta^2 & 0 & 0\\
0 & -\dot\theta^2 & 0\\
0&0&0
\end{bmatrix}
\]

Now add:

\[
[\dot\omega]^\times + ([\omega]^\times)^2
=
\begin{bmatrix}
-\dot\theta^2 & -\ddot\theta & 0\\
\ddot\theta & -\dot\theta^2 & 0\\
0&0&0
\end{bmatrix}
\]

---

## Final Match (Second Identity Verified)

\[
\boxed{
C_i^{\,B}\ddot C_B^{\,i}
=
[\dot\omega]^\times + \big([\omega]^\times\big)^2
}
\]